      "textEn": "147\n\nis equal. The governments afflicted by pandemics are slowly ruining all the happiness of human society. Therefore, it is the duty of Vaishnava preachers to perform actions on the supreme position of Bhagavat, so that they can clearly\ngive directions to humanity and not be corrupted or\nattracted by the material opulence given to saints. All intelligent men who cannot directly accept the method of devotion,\nshould at least be so educated that they accept the guidance of a devotee of God of the highest order,\nby giving recognition. In this way, human society can be well organized, so that not only\nall humans but also animals, birds, and trees can progress in life and for the sake of joy and knowledge,\nthey can gradually return to the abode of God for their daily lives. Srila Bhaktisiddhanth Saraswati Thakur has emphasized that those who are sincerely desirous of attaining perfection in Krishna consciousness should live in the Vaishnava community.\nSrila Prabhupada has also mentioned in his\nbooks many times that until the state of complete Krishna consciousness is attained,\nit is not possible, until pure devotees are taken refuge in the Krishna consciousness-filled\ncommunities established by the International Krishna Consciousness Association throughout the world. Srila Bhaktisiddhanth Saraswati Thakur has\nemphasized that it does not mean that spiritual life is limited to those living in the temple complex\nand to the celibates. The devotees of the Grihastha Ashram can also regularly attend the temple festivals and take refuge in the Vaishnava community. Those who are living a domestic life, they should\nwant to see the idol of God daily, chant his name in front of them, and\nlisten to the discussions of scholars on the Bhagavad Gita and the Bhagavata.\nAny householder who regularly takes advantage of these spiritual facilities\nand follows the rules of spiritual life—not eating meat, not having illegal sexual\npractices, not gambling, 