त्य",
      "textEn": "156\n\nFor this, a suitable residence is created. A civilized person would want to live in a clean place. He cannot live in a contaminated place. Educated people in Western countries are now strongly opposing the pollution of water and air by urban industrial establishments. They are demanding their right to live in a clean place. Similarly, Lord Krishna is the most auspicious person, therefore he would neither want to live in a corrupt heart,\nnor would he appear in the corrupt mind of a bound soul. When a devotee takes refuge in Lord Krishna and\nbecomes a God-loving person through the direct experience of Krishna's all-attractive nature, then God makes such a devotee\nhis abode. According to Srila Jiva Goswami—yet, by such love, by this, always, by the supreme control, he is always praised.\nTherefore, he is also the destroyer of the obstacles. If a devotee remains immersed in the divine loving devotion of Lord Krishna, then he\nthrough this service, directly or indirectly, keeps describing the glory of God.\nTherefore, if\nhe remains engaged in the service of God, even with half-hearted devotion, chanting the name of Krishna,\nthen by the grace of God, all the sins of his heart are washed away. As it is said in Shrimad Bhagavatam\n(2.1.11)—\n\nEtanirvidyamanamanam ichchataam akutobhayam. Yoginam nrip nirnitam harinaramanukirtanam. “Hey Rajan! By following the path of great men, continuous chanting of the name of God is the path to success for all.\nIt is a path to success without doubt and without fear. It includes all those who are free from all material desires, who are desirous of material pleasures, and also those who are satisfied with the self through the power of divine knowledge.\"\nTherefore, if someone has not reached the position of divine love and devotion, but chants the name of Krishna, then\nhe too will be freed from all sins. In the sixth canto of Shrimad Bhagavat, while presenting the essence of the life history of Ajamila, Srila Prabhupada has explained in detail that the holy name has the power to purify even an ordinary person.\nSrila Vishwanath Chakravarti Thakur has described a beautiful method to control God. Mother\nYashoda had tied the child Krishna with a rope and a pestle. Krishna, his devotees' unthinkable"
