      "textEn": "161\n\nThe senses are engaged in measuring the material objects. King Nimi, from the nine Yoginis, now\nwants to know completely from Shri Antariksha about the true nature of that Maya, which compels the bound soul\nto turn away from Krishna-bhava-anamrita and forces them to kneel before the material objects that are deceptive. Nanutrupe yuksanuyushmaadvacho harikathamrutam. The heat of the world, the burning of the mortal, is the medicine. 2. Meaning of the word:\n\nNot dissatisfied—I am still not satisfied; Jushan—being busy; Yushmat—yours; Vachah—in words; Harikatha—stories of Lord Hari; Amrutam—nectar; Sansar—of the world; Tapah—by suffering; Nistaptah—being tormented; Martyah—a mortal human; Tat-\nTapah—of that suffering; Bheshajam—medicine I.\n\nAlthough I am relishing the nectar of the glory of God being told by you,\nStill my thirst is not quenched. Such nectarous stories of God and his devotees, the world\nis tormented by three afflictions, for bound souls like me, they are working as medicine.\nMeaning: According to Srila Sridhar Swami, it can be argued that since the characteristics of a devotee of God\nhave already been described in detail, therefore, by attaining the position described in the previous verse,\na person can make his life successful, so what is the need to ask further questions? But Harikathamrutam—that is, the stories of God and his devotees are so delightful and beautiful that\neven after salvation, no one can stop listening to them. In this regard, Shri Chaitanya Mahaprabhu has\nquoted the following verse—\n\nAtmaramashcha munayo nirgrantha apyururumre. Kurvantyahatukam bhaktiim itthambhutaguno harih. “Those who are self-realized and not attracted to external material desires, they too are attracted to that Shri Krishna's\ndevotion through love, whose qualities are divine and whose actions are wonderful. Lord Hari is called Krishna\nbecause his limbs are divinely attractive.\n” (Bhagavat 1.7.10) If once\nthe disease gets cured, then there is no need for medicine, but at the supreme position, work"
